    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d321">

                <pb facs="0481" n="393" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg393"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/2805: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-28T15:00:00+01:00"
                            >November 28, 1918—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10.48 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3222. Your 1221, November 18, 7 p.m.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d321-f1"/> Query 4.
                    Danish press on November 13 reported on the aversion [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >assurance?</hi>] of a Vienna newspaper, that Roumania had sent Hungary an
                    ultimatum demanding that Siebenbuergen be immediately evacuated and left to the
                    Roumanian Crown. Further details not given. Danish press reports this morning
                    that Roumanian forces have actually occupied extensive Hungarian territories,
                    and that fears are expressed in Budapest that the occupation will include all
                    districts up to the capital. Repeated to House, referring his 112, November 16,
                    3 p.m. to Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d321-f1" n="13" xml:id="d321-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it transmitted the queries listed in telegram No. 112, Nov. 16.
                    1918, 3 p.m., from Colonel House, <ref target="frus1919Parisv01#pg_197">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 197</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
